{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"CHANGES REQUIRED on a4d17373b49e1ed3958fe92d03397dfc853c3283: independent accuracy review found four documentation defects. The structured-output module said only provider calls occur there although deterministic scoring/artifact work also occurs; only those calls are live. It also attributed default exclusion to both external and llm_live, although external excludes while llm_live routes provider-matrix selection, and it omitted the distinction between an arm-level credential skip and uncredentialed cells recorded as unmeasured. The verified-fake module referred to one test although it defines four. The workflow module implied both tests traverse review_skeleton although the second invokes live plan review. Corrections are limited to those docstrings; a fresh exact-SHA independent receipt is required."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788901862350707001,"uuid":"5a233632-29cd-4ac4-94ae-5a6f3a690e43"}